# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  SPECTRAVEIN Backend v2.0 — Cloud-Native Environment Configuration
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# Instructions:
# 1. Copy this file to .env for local development
# 2. For Azure App Service: Set these in Configuration > Application Settings
# 3. For Docker: Pass via --env-file or docker-compose.yml
#
# Security: Never commit .env to version control! (.env is in .gitignore)
#

# ── CORS Configuration (CRITICAL FOR PRODUCTION) ────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated list of allowed frontend origins.
# ⚠️  SECURITY: Do NOT use "*" wildcard in production!
#
# Local Development:
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000
#
# Production Example:
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://spectravein.vercel.app,https://www.spectravein.com
#
# Investor Demo (Add temporary domains as needed):
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://spectravein.vercel.app,https://demo.spectravein.com

# ── Database Configuration (Future: Azure PostgreSQL) ────────────────────────
# Leave blank for CSV-based data loading (current phase)
# Set to PostgreSQL connection string when migrating to Phase 2
#
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@spectravein-db.postgres.database.azure.com:5432/spectravein

# ── Application Metadata ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These can usually be left at defaults
#
APP_NAME=SPECTRAVEIN Mining Intelligence API
APP_VERSION=2.0.0
ENVIRONMENT=development
# Options: development, staging, production

# ── Logging Configuration ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
LOG_LEVEL=INFO
# Options: DEBUG, INFO, WARNING, ERROR, CRITICAL

# ── Data Source ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Path to the ML-labeled asteroid dataset (relative to backend/ directory)
CSV_PATH=asteroid_labeled.csv
